OL,3,GNEWSACar scam victim 'nearly passed    
OL,4,Aout' when he realised he'd lost #6,000 
OL,6,FDenis Crampton thought he had found the
OL,7,Fperfect car for his wife while looking 
OL,8,Fonline.                                
OL,10,FA blue Range Rover Evoque was being    
OL,11,Fadvertised for #6,250 by a private     
OL,12,Fseller on eBay.                        
OL,14,FDenis believed he had carried out all  
OL,15,Fof the the necessary checks before     
OL,16,Fagreeing to purchase the vehicle.      
OL,18,FCrucially, however, the 72-year-old was
OL,19,Fpersuaded to pay upfront before making 
OL,20,Fthe three-and-a-half-hour rail journey 
OL,21,Ffrom Stockport to Bristol Temple Meads 
OL,22,Fto collect the car.                    
